  "question": {
    "text": "Electron beam used in an electron microscope, when accelerated by a voltage of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kV</mi></math>&nbsp;has a de-Broglie wavelength of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. If the voltage is increased to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kV</mi></math>&nbsp;then the de-Broglie wavelength associated with the electron beam would be:",
